---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const editor = 'https://composer-launch-kit.loftwah.workers.dev';
const examples = [
  {file:'river-typography',title:'Let the words lead.',name:'River · typography',description:'A clear name, a short introduction and deliberate colour. No image needed.'},
  {file:'night-signal-music',title:'Give the music a face.',name:'Night Signal · creative',description:'A creative treatment with room for an existing cover or illustration.'},
  {file:'field-notes-editorial',title:'Use the whole picture.',name:'Field Notes · editorial',description:'A banner composition that keeps the artwork distinct from the exact typeset copy.'},
];
---
<Base title="Launch Kit" description="Make a profile card, app icons or a complete launch package locally. Inspect the actual output, then deliberately apply and publish it.">
  <div class="kit-intro">
    <h1>Your identity.<br/>Ready to share.</h1>
    <div><p class="lede">Make a profile card with your exact words and your own artwork. Or start with type alone. Inspect the PNG you’ll actually use.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={editor+'/profile.html'}>Make a profile card</a><a class="button secondary" href="#choose-output">Make icons or a package</a></div>
    <p class="small">Local processing. No account required. Your original artwork stays on your device.</p></div>
  </div>
  <section class="kit-examples" aria-label="Finished profile card examples">
    {examples.map((example)=><figure><a href={'/launch-kit/cards/'+example.file+'.png'}><img src={'/launch-kit/cards/'+example.file+'.png'} width="1200" height="630" alt={example.name+' — fictional finished profile card'} loading="eager"/></a><figcaption><h2>{example.title}</h2><p>{example.description}</p><a href={editor+'/profile.html?example='+example.file}>Try this fictional example ↗</a></figcaption></figure>)}
  </section>
  <section id="choose-output" class="kit-outputs">
    <h2>Start with what you need.</h2>
    <dl>
      <div><dt><a href={editor+'/profile.html'}>Profile or social card ↗</a></dt><dd>The image people see when your profile link is shared. Choose type, portrait, banner or a combination. Compare a few presets before selecting one.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href={editor+'/?operation=icons'}>App icons ↗</a></dt><dd>A favicon for browser tabs, an app icon for home screens, and a maskable icon with space for the device’s own crop.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href={editor+'/'}>Complete launch package ↗</a></dt><dd>Icons, a shared-link image, a web manifest and installation notes together. Keep the full-package workflow when you need the whole set.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section id="profile-publication" class="kit-publication">
    <div><h2>From your profile<br/>to its public image.</h2><p>In <a href="/_emdash/admin/plugins/composer-miniapps/apps?app=showcase">Linkarooie’s owner settings</a>, download a profile snapshot and open the card editor in a separate tab. Your unsaved work stays in place.</p><p>Import the snapshot, choose a treatment and any local artwork, then render. The large preview and feed preview show the encoded PNG. Select and download only when you’re happy with it.</p></div>
    <div><ol><li><strong>Rendered locally.</strong> Review the image and save its recipe. Original source images are not silently included.</li><li><strong>Prepared for publication.</strong> An agent copies the selected PNG into Linkarooie with an immutable name, reviews and deploys that asset through the existing release route.</li><li><strong>Published deliberately.</strong> Import the adoption receipt in owner settings. Compare current and proposed images, then publish. A changed profile revision requires a fresh card.</li><li><strong>Served result verified.</strong> Check the public page, metadata, image type, dimensions and exact bytes. Restore the previously approved image if needed.</li></ol><p class="small">Local files and copied commands are preparation. Publication and public verification are separate online actions.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="kit-agent"><h2>The same renderer, from a command.</h2><p>A local browser adapter reads the same versioned recipe as the editor. Fonts and selected artwork come from local files. After dependencies are available, rendering works with external requests blocked.</p><pre><code>pnpm render public/examples/river-typography.json output/river --compare</code></pre><p><a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer-launch-kit/blob/main/docs/profile-cards.md">Local commands, presets and recipes ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer-showcase/blob/main/docs/launch-kit-publication.md">Asset preparation and publication ↗</a></p><details><summary>Optional AI artwork</summary><p>The normal workflow requires no model subscription. Optional artwork runs in a trusted local process with explicit enablement, a selected provider key, a deliberate prompt and a configured usage limit. Exact names, handles and copy are always composed locally. The public editor holds no provider credentials.</p><p>One fictional music background was generated through that adapter and then typeset locally. <a href="https://composer-launch-kit.loftwah.workers.dev/profile.html?example=night-signal-artwork">Inspect and edit the finished example ↗</a></p><a href="/launch-kit/cards/night-signal-artwork.png"><img src="/launch-kit/cards/night-signal-artwork.png" width="1200" height="630" alt="Fictional Night Signal card with a locally typeset name beside optional generated radio and moth artwork" loading="lazy" style="max-width:600px;width:100%;height:auto"/></a></details></section>
  <section><h2>Keep the complete-package workflow.</h2><p>The fictional Night Signal timer demonstrates the original portable ZIP → Composer import → working app route. You can still inspect a full package and adopt selected branding into a separate app draft.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/init/launch-kit">Import a launch package</a><a href="/launch-kit/example/">Try the published timer</a><a href="https://share.loftwah.com/">Inspect with Link Check ↗</a></div><p class="small">Browser checks and served files remain separate from physical installation, screen-reader use, native social-platform unfurls and owner artistic approval.</p></section>
</Base>
<style>
  .kit-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:end;padding-block:32px 48px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border)}
  .kit-intro h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,6.5vw,5.5rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0}.kit-intro .lede{margin-top:0}.kit-intro .small{margin-bottom:0}
  section{margin-top:48px;padding-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}
  .kit-examples{border-top:0;padding-top:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;margin-top:32px}.kit-examples figure{margin:0;min-width:0}.kit-examples img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.kit-examples h2{font-size:1.25rem;margin-block:20px 10px}.kit-examples p{font-size:1rem}.kit-examples figcaption>a{min-height:44px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center}
  .kit-outputs dl{margin:0}.kit-outputs dl>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:24px;padding-block:24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border)}.kit-outputs dt{font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:650}.kit-outputs dd{margin:0;max-width:65ch}
  .kit-publication{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:48px}.kit-publication h2{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.15}.kit-publication ol{margin-top:0;padding-left:24px}.kit-publication li{padding-left:8px;margin-bottom:20px}.kit-agent pre{padding:20px;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-border)}details summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:list-item;padding-block:10px}
  @media(max-width:850px){.kit-intro,.kit-publication{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:28px}.kit-examples{grid-template-columns:1fr}.kit-examples figure{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:24px}.kit-examples h2{margin-top:0}}
  @media(max-width:550px){.kit-intro{padding-top:16px}.kit-intro h1{font-size:3.25rem}.kit-examples figure,.kit-outputs dl>div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}.kit-examples h2{margin-top:12px}section{margin-top:36px}}
</style>
